{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Cigarettes and whiskey and [C]wild wild [G]women
They'll drive you crazy they'll [A7]drive you [D7]insane
[G]Cigarettes and whiskey and [C]wild wild [G]women
They'll drive you crazy they'll [D7]drive you [G7]insane
Once I was happy and [C]had a good [G]wife
I had enough money to [A7]last me for [D7]life
I [G]met with a gal and we [C]went on a [G]spree
She taught me smoking and [D7]drinking [G]whiskey
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And now I’m feeble and broken with age
The lines on my face make a well written page
I'm weaving this story how sadly how true
On women and whiskey and what they can do
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Write on the cross at the head of my grave
For women and whiskey here lies a poor slave
Take warning dear stranger take warning dear friend
